Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:26:43 -0500
Subject: feat: Shift-click on any link opens it in a peek (S-488)

A peek opened only for a link leaving a pinned tab's site. Shift-click on
any link, from any tab of a normal window, to any site, now opens it in a
peek over the page, as Arc's Shift-click does; a link that opens a page of
its own (target=_blank) too. Chromium gave Shift-click a new window; the
context menu's Open Link in New Window is the browser's own and keeps it.

The decision is made where a pin's new-tab links already peek, at the top
of Navigate(): a NEW_WINDOW link, renderer-initiated with the user's
gesture, to an http(s) page, from a tab of the window's strip (not from a
peek's own page), with the setting on. The peek is the same one a pin
opens: its jar, its Open as Tab and Open in Split View.

Settings > Stedding > Peek and little windows > "Shift-click a link to
peek at it" (stedding.peek.shift_click), on by default; off, Shift-click
opens a window again.

Why: GitHub discussion 115; the owner asked for the requests that could
ship in 0.5.1 (2026-11-14). Spec: peek P27, settings T63.
Removable when: never; Stedding's own way to open a peek.
